{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on 6780e0cd for OPS-2 (60f5b713).\n\n1. Unchanged names. My request was wrong: no name refuses an\nunchanged bundle at main 28aa0446. Do not add a refusal. Skip the\nname. When the bundle SHA and the config bytes both equal the\nprevious receipt, deploy.mjs prints the name as `unchanged`, sends\nnothing for that name, writes no receipt for it and deploys the\nother names. The command exits 0. The rule holds for all five\nnames. A changed SCREEN_HOSTS changes the config bytes, so a\nmapping change still deploys. One test covers a run with one\nunchanged name and one changed name. A refusal would stop a\nfive-name run whenever one bundle is the same. Most landings leave\nat least one bundle the same.\n\n2. Unmapped host. Keep the fixed host `unmapped-smoke.\u003cparent\ndomain\u003e` and take no third argument. The zone holds a proxied\nwildcard record for `*.inguz.space`. On 12 November at 06:38 a read\nof `other.inguz.space` reached the Worker and returned 404. Keep\nthe refusal for a host that is a tracked mapping.\n\nThe 403 read stands as you wrote it.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}